<article class="env-lemma" id="02OL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02OL">Lemma <span data-tag="02OL">31.4.6</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent sheaf on $X$. The set of coherent subsheaves </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \{  \mathcal{K} \subset \mathcal{F} \mid \text{Supp}(\mathcal{K})\text{ is nowhere dense in }\text{Supp}(\mathcal{F}) \}   \]
</div>
  <p> has a maximal element $\mathcal{K}$. Setting $\mathcal{F}' = \mathcal{F}/\mathcal{K}$ we have the following </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\text{Supp}(\mathcal{F}') = \text{Supp}(\mathcal{F})$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}'$ has no embedded associated points, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a dense open $U \subset X$ such that $U \cap \text{Supp}(\mathcal{F})$ is dense in $\text{Supp}(\mathcal{F})$ and $\mathcal{F}'|_ U \cong \mathcal{F}|_ U$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/02M6" data-tag="02M6">10.67.2</a> and <a href="/tag/02M7" data-tag="02M7">10.67.3</a>. Note that $U$ can be taken as the complement of the closure of the set of embedded associated points of $\mathcal{F}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>